  beta  could be red or it could be kind of a  mess traditional class items for all  more than one of you pointed out in the  comments after the reveal that we didn't  see any medical or supply crates on the  ground  it turns out that they are in the game  players can customize primary weapons  equipment  secondary weapons and throwables most  notable is that under the equipment slot  now anybody can carry a medical crate or  a supply crate that's a pretty massive  change from previous class specific  roles in battlefield  and shows that even though specialists  generally do fall under that traditional  class system  that system's reliance on people picking  the right class at the right time for  the right situation  seems kind of diminished will  specialists be visually confusing  it looks like squads are limited to four  players but there's no limit to the  types of specialists they can take with  them  you might have a full stack team of  folks who's the medic and then run  around and encounter an enemy team doing  the same strategy  this is reminiscent of the old revive  trains in previous battlefield games  where teams of medics would just keep  reviving each other  and now that any specialist can pick any  weapon that might be an even more  dominant strategy  it also might just get confusing with so  many specialists that look exactly the  same running around  in the blog post dice appears to be  banking on skins making the players look  vastly different  but it's also clear they haven't fully  figured this out yet and are  experimenting with friend faux  recognition  using traditional icons and other  options  just that one person gets the wingsuit  from previous trailers it seems  very much like the featured specialist  listed as sundance was the only person  with a wingsuit and later in developer  interviews they seemed to confirm that  but now we have it in writing there's  only one specialist with this ability  it seems like a pretty big advantage for  sundance who can chase down tornadoes  and use them to jet  far distances across the map even more  useful on maps that don't have tall  buildings  and i guess everybody else just has to  deal with a parachute  building interiors are not that  extensive which could be good or bad  battlefield 2042 looks like it has some  fantastic city maps such as kaleidoscope  in south korea  and hourglass in doha those buildings  will mostly just be used to get up high  though  and pretty much consist of a lobby and a  rooftop you can get to the top by way of  elevators and zip lines  the justification for lack of interior  floors is to prevent distractions from  the rest of the map  which could be fair and reasonable but  it could also be more fun to have  objectives inside of buildings  some other maps will have those  interiors like the colossus ship on  discarded  if this is a good design decision or not  it really depends on how maps  use those skyscrapers and if lots of  players do what they normally do  which is grab a sniper rifle head to the  top and snipe now that's a lot of fun  but not very productive inside  objectives reduce the incentive for  players to do that  expanded out of bounds an issue with  skyscrapers in the past is how many  rooftops were out of bounds  the next posting has more to do with  jets and vehicles but it's a good sign  that the out-of-bounds area of maps have  been pushed further out that means more  room to roam for vehicles and jets but  also players  the vehicle call-in system we finally  got clarification on when players will  be able to call in vehicles players were  trying to figure this out since the  reveal  and see if it was tied to a point system  like more recent battlefield games or  two capturing objectives  the answer is that all players can call  in vehicle drops based on a specific  budget assigned to their team  which changes based on the map and the  mode once you use this ability there's a  cooldown to prevent you from spamming it  so it sounds like there's a system in  place to limit your team from calling in  all tanks for example  based on how much each one costs but if  i were a betting man  you'll probably be able to call in  smaller transport vehicles most of the  time  so you don't get stranded unfortunately  this section also drops some bad news  direct spawning from the deploy screen  into vehicles and air assets is  back i don't know many older battlefield  players who like this system because  we want the runways man it's just so  immersion breaking to spawn into  vehicles directly  and also undermines the value of  capturing objectives like an airfield  maybe newer battlefield players like  this  i don't know how do you feel about it  let me know in the comments below  alright back to good news the vehicle  calling system includes robot dog  so many people wanted to know more about  the robot dog from the trailer  and if it was tied to boris the  specialist most liked the classic  engineer  the answer is that the robot dog's name  is ranger and it's tied to the colin  tablet  ranger can therefore be dropped in by  anyone but not at any time that's  limited by team points as mentioned  earlier ranger seems to be autonomous  and follows the player until issued  orders to scout a location  return to you or follow ranger will also  sacrifice its life for you  it can apparently self-destruct the  robot dog falls under the light unit  category  and goes down easily but it's confirmed  that you can also use it as jeep stuff  you monster  [Music]  all right lightning round on random  vehicle info there wasn't a lot more  here on vehicles but one thing the post  confirmed is that factions will have  their own vehicles  and there are some shared in between  them but at this time there are no naval  maps  how ai soldiers really work we now have  more detail on how ai soldiers will  operate  it sounds like they'll try to blend in  and do many of the same things you're  gonna do  like calling in vehicles capping  objectives throwing grenades and  reviving you  unlike players they cannot be  specialists or use specialist abilities  like the wingsuit  in conquest and breakthrough there's a  cap on how many ai soldiers can be on a  map at a time  generally fewer than the number of human  players that are also there  but that can change apparently when a  match is filling up or is nearly empty  one specific example cited in the post  is that if there's a match that's 120  verse 128  eight bots will join one side to balance  the teams you cannot opt out of bots and  matches and even in solo mode you'll  still be online with bots  cross everything is confirmed  battlefield 2042  is working on cross-platform play and  we'll have testing going on later this  summer  the game will also have cross a between  different consoles like xbox and  playstation  as well as pc which is amazing and  finally  penguins have been confirmed on the  breakaway map they are  it's great i have nothing more to say  about this you do not have to wait long  for battlefield 2042 announcements ea  play live on july 22nd is already  teasing something new from ripple effect  formerly dice la and we already know  2042 will have the  not battle royale mode called hazard  zone as well as remastered fan favorite  maps from previous games  dammavan peak please for more  battlefield 2042 news head on over to  gamespot's youtube page  thanks for watching  you

